 "https://www.timeout.com/bangkok/th/attractions/วัดโพธิ์"}, {"title": "www.trueplookpanya.com", "url": "https://www.trueplookpanya.com/game/quiz/play/193"}]}, "The search returned one clear answer: the temple of the 10th reign is **วัดวชิรธรรมสาธิตวรวิหาร (Wat Witsundhamsathit Worawihan)**, also called วัดทุ่งสาธิต, in Bangkok. TrueID's travel article identifies it as the royal temple of King Rama X, and it is in Bangkok.\n\nOther results cover the broader tradition:\n- A TrueID guide lists the royal temples of Rama I through Rama X, one for each reign in Bangkok. The snippet I saw only reached Rama I's temple, so I could not confirm the full list.\n- Wat Pho (วัดพระเชตุพนวิมลมังคลาราม) is the royal temple of Rama I.\n- Thai kings have traditionally built personal temples since the reign of Rama I, although sometimes a king adopted and restored a temple built by someone else.\n\nThe results are thin. Only one source names the Rama X temple, and the search did not return an official palace or government page to confirm it. If accuracy matters, verify against an official source before relying on it."], "durationSeconds": 5.06954275, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01A6XZQ4rR5phJUMXn6VBXKq", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
